    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i don't know if i want to find a rhythm anymore. it just feels like a long, tiring performance that i didn't audition for. sometimes i look at the sunset or the way the seasons change and i think... they don't struggle like this. they just finish their cycle. they just fade out when the time is right. it seems so much more peaceful than this constant, heavy effort to exist in a world that doesn't want me.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
